<title>UK: Cuba 1996 sugar exports sharply higher yr/yr - ISO.</title>
<headline>Cuba 1996 sugar exports sharply higher yr/yr - ISO.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cuba exported 3.83 million tonnes of sugar in 1996, sharply up from the 2.60 million exported the previous year, the International Sugar Organization (ISO) said on Friday.</p>
<p>Russia took the vast majority of the 1996 exports with 1.83 million tonnes, more than double the amount it imported in 1995, the ISO said.</p>
<p>ISO data showed China came in second place in 1996, importing 432,417 tonnes of Cuban sugar, followed by Morocco with 206,866 tonnes. --Jeremy Smith, London Newsroom +44 171 542 8064</p>
</text>
